BP-DEBUG: fix for #17
https://github.com/teknoplop/anneq/issues/17

Weight dumps and "press a key" pauses run on every trial, and they call print_weights() with its
layer arguments swapped, reading the input layer's NULL weight pointers. Harmless on real-mode DOS
(it reads low memory), a segfault on a hosted OS. Removed. The third hunk is inside #ifdef DEBUG
and only matters for debug builds.

Applies to the sources prepared by src/tools/prepare.py (wrapped lines rejoined,
names lower-cased), not to src/borland/ directly:
  patch -p1 -d <prep dir> < src/fixes/BP-DEBUG.patch

--- a/bpbc.c
+++ b/bpbc.c
@@ -120,13 +120,8 @@
                 getch();
                 clrscr();
                 #endif
+                                        /* Fix #17: debug weight dump (arguments swapped) and key wait removed
+                                         * https://github.com/teknoplop/anneq/issues/17 */
-                                        gotoxy(1, 1);
-                        print_weights(ann.layer_1, ann.layer_0, ann.nodes_0+1, ann.nodes_1);
-                        print_weights(ann.layer_2, ann.layer_1, ann.nodes_1+1, ann.nodes_2);
-                        print_weights(ann.layer_3, ann.layer_2, ann.nodes_2+1, ann.nodes_3);
-                        printf("\n");
-                        while(!kbhit());
-                        getch();
 
 /* Initialise the network */
 
@@ -170,13 +165,8 @@
                 ann.layer_1[ann.nodes_1].output = -1.0;
                 ann.layer_2[ann.nodes_2].output = -1.0;
 
+                        /* Fix #17: debug weight dump (arguments swapped) and key wait removed
+                         * https://github.com/teknoplop/anneq/issues/17 */
-                        gotoxy(1, 1);
-                        print_weights(ann.layer_1, ann.layer_0, ann.nodes_0+1, ann.nodes_1);
-                        print_weights(ann.layer_2, ann.layer_1, ann.nodes_1+1, ann.nodes_2);
-                        print_weights(ann.layer_3, ann.layer_2, ann.nodes_2+1, ann.nodes_3);
-                        printf("\n");
-                        while(!kbhit());
-                        getch();
 
 /* Start training */
 
